Introduction
Email Extractor Automation is a Python project that automates the process of extracting email addresses from a text file.

In real life, people often receive large text documents, reports, or notes containing email addresses. Manually searching and copying each email can take time. This project solves that problem by automatically finding all valid email addresses and saving them into a separate file.

Main Purpose
The main purpose of this project is to automate a repetitive task using Python.

The selected automation task is:

Extract all email addresses from a .txt file and save them into another file.

How It Works
The program starts with a menu.
A sample input file is created automatically if it does not exist.
The user can view the input file.
The user can add more text into the input file.
The program extracts email addresses using regular expressions.
Duplicate emails are removed.
Extracted emails are saved in extracted_emails.txt.
A detailed report is generated in automation_report.txt.
Important Python Concepts Used
1. Regular Expressions
Regular expressions are used to search for email address patterns.

2. File Handling
File handling is used to read and write text files.

3. Functions
Functions are used to keep the code clean and reusable.

4. Loops
A while loop is used to show the menu repeatedly.

5. Conditional Statements
If-elif-else statements are used to process menu options.

6. Pathlib
Pathlib is used for file path management.

7. DateTime
The datetime module is used to add date and time to the automation report.

